e":"柿崎商店 海鮮工房","summary":"A fishmonger’s upstairs canteen where Hokkaidō seafood is served with unusually little distance between wholesale counter and bowl.","whyWorthwhile":"The attraction is not refinement: it is access to strong raw material at a price and breadth difficult to reproduce in an ordinary city restaurant.","entityType":"food","countryCode":"JP","country":"Japan","region":"Hokkaido","locality":"Yoichi","categories":["food-drink","seafood-and-fishing-port-food"],"subcategories":["seafood-and-fishing-port-food"],"tags":["seafood bowls","fishmonger","uni","Yoichi","Uni-don, ikura-don, grilled fish set meals, seasonal shellfish"],"tier":"A","geometryType":"Point","centroid":[140.792849,43.186536],"bbox":[140.792849,43.186536,140.792849,43.186536],"customNamespace":"food","customFacets":{"food.primaryCategory":"Seafood & Fishing-Port Food","food.japanRegion":"Hokkaido","food.value":"exceptional","food.reservationClass":"walk-in","food.englishAccess":"B"},"cardSignals":["Seafood & Fishing Port Food","English B","Reservation: walk in"],"latestExternalRating":null,"coverImage":null,"demo":false},{"id":"727e9ea3-6d74-546f-a4be-60567bd393ee","slug":"ginneko","name":"Ginneko","localName":"焼鳥専門ぎんねこ","summary":"A single bird preparation—roasted over charcoal and lacquered with a long-used tare—functions as an unusually durable local dish rather than generic yakitori.","whyWorthwhile":"Its strongest decision-relevant feature is access to Asahikawa's half-chicken charcoal-roasted 'shinkoyaki'. The recommended visit is: Reserve one shinkoyaki per suitable group and add a few skewers rather than over-ordering.","entityType":"food","countryCode":"JP","country":"Japan","region":"Hokkaido","locality":"Asahikawa","categories":["food-drink","meat-grill"],"subcategories":["meat-grill"],"tags":["shinkoyaki","chicken","post-war local specialist"],"tier":"B","geometryType":"Point","centroid":[142.360811,43.769974],"bbox":[142.360811,43.769974,142.360811,43.769974],"customName